      "title": "Carrier Q3 Earnings & Sales Beat on HVAC Demand, Tariff Refunds",
      "summary": "Carrier Global (CARR) delivered exceptional Q3 2026 results with adjusted EPS up 30% to 87 cents and sales growth of 12% to $6.26 billion, driven by surging commercial HVAC orders (60% increase) and explosive data-center demand (300% jump). The company raised 2026 sales guidance to $23.8-$24 billion with record backlog of $8.5 billion. However, a $3.1 billion goodwill impairment charge resulted in a GAAP loss, causing the stock to plunge 7.2% in pre-market trading.",
